# Env vars for running studios/vcut in HOSTED mode (the public vcut.io web deploy — real accounts,
# per-user project ownership). Desktop, local dev, and the native mobile shell need none of this:
# leaving every one of these unset is what makes this app behave exactly as it always did before
# hosted mode existed (see _lib/auth.ts's own VCUT_HOSTED doc comment).
#
# The NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed vars below are inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD time, not read
# at container start — see the Dockerfile's own comment on this. Setting them only as runtime
# variables (Railway's dashboard/CLI env vars, set after the image is already built) silently ships a
# build where sign-in no-ops for every visitor.

# Turns on hosted mode server-side: real bearer-token auth required, ownership checks on every
# project-scoped route, Auto Captions/Remove Object credit-gated using the server-owned keys below
# instead of a per-installation saved key (see _lib/localOnly.ts's hostedCreditGatedRoute and
# _lib/credits.ts).
VCUT_HOSTED=true

# Same flag, client-side — gates the marketing landing page vs. the local project dashboard at `/`,
# and switches packages/vcut/src/api/client.ts's apiFetch to attach a Supabase bearer token.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VCUT_HOSTED=true

# From your Supabase project's Settings -> API. The anon key is safe to expose to a browser by
# design (Postgres row-level security is what actually protects data, not keeping this secret) —
# still passed as a Docker build-arg rather than committed here, so this file can stay identical
# across every environment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Server-only — grants full, RLS-bypassing database access (packages/auth/src/server.ts). A genuine
# secret: never NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed, never a build arg, never committed. Set with
# `railway variables --set SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=... --service vcut`, not committed here.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Optional — caps total simultaneous exports on this one machine (see export/route.ts's own comment
# on why this can't be spread across multiple machines). Defaults to 2 if unset; raise it only after
# actually confirming the deployed machine's CPU/RAM can take more concurrent Chromium+FFmpeg work.
VCUT_MAX_CONCURRENT_EXPORTS=2

# Billing (see app/api/vcut/billing/*/route.ts, _lib/stripe.ts, _lib/profiles.ts) — VCut Pro is paid
# for centrally, one Stripe account for every user on every platform (web, desktop, mobile all call
# this same hosted deployment for these four routes specifically). All three are genuine secrets: set
# with `railway variables --set KEY=value --service vcut`, never committed, never a NEXT_PUBLIC_-
# prefixed build arg.
#
# From the Stripe dashboard's API keys page (use a TEST mode key while developing).
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# From the webhook endpoint you register in the Stripe dashboard pointing at
# https://<your-deploy>/api/vcut/billing/webhook — shown once, when you create that endpoint.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# The Price id (not Product id) of the "VCut Pro" recurring price you create in the Stripe dashboard's
# Product catalog. Differs between Stripe test mode and live mode — don't reuse one for the other.
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=price_...

# Auto Captions AND Remove Object in hosted mode — ONE VCut-owned Replicate token funding every
# hosted tenant's usage on BOTH features (Captions runs Replicate's own openai/whisper model; metered
# by credits either way — see _lib/credits.ts's own doc comment on why a shared token is safe here in
# a way a shared token wasn't before credits existed). Separate from any personal token you may have
# saved locally via the Inspector's own settings UI (that UI stays disabled in hosted mode — see
# _lib/inpaintEnvFile.ts's VCUT_HOSTED branches, including getReplicateToken for Captions' own use).
# Only Replicate is enabled in hosted mode (fal.ai isn't; "local" — real Python ML inference on the
# shared production box — never can be, see inpaint/route.ts's runLocalPrediction).
VCUT_HOSTED_REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=r8_...
